program	errors/borrowing_struct_type_positions.saw
triple	arm64-apple-darwin
twin	differs
expect	error
build	refused	field `it` of `Holder` may not name a borrowing struct: `BagIterator` is a `borrows struct`, and a borrowing struct holds a LENT PLACE, so its values live only inside their window — the extent is the `for` statement, which is what makes the borrow trackable without a lifetime. A type argument, an existential, a field, a parameter and a plain return each outlive the window, so none of them can name one — which is what makes a generic identity wrapper unwritable rather than caught
meets_expect	yes
